    <string name="onb_title_1">The universe has a language</string>
    <string name="onb_body_1">Richard Feynman invented a way to draw how particles interact. With these drawings physicists calculate everything from the colour of the sky to what happens at CERN.</string>
    <string name="onb_title_2">Three letters to begin</string>
    <string name="onb_body_2">Each line is a particle. Time moves from left to right.</string>
    <string name="onb_title_3">Learn by doing</string>
    <string name="onb_body_3">Decode diagrams, build them with your own hands and hunt down mistakes. Each challenge takes 2 to 5 minutes, and the physics explains why your solution works.</string>
